    id: "x1-1-1r9cdu1",
    chapter: 1,
    block: 1,
    stem: "A 22-year-old patient is involved. You arrive at a crowded emergency department with a stable patient. The charge nurse points to a hallway bed and walks away without taking report. The MOST appropriate action is to:",
    choices: [
      "Document that the nurse assumed care at the moment you arrived",
      "Move the patient to the bed and leave the written report at the desk",
      "Stay with the patient and give verbal report to a nurse or physician",
      "Return the patient to the ambulance until a treatment room opens",
    ],
    answer: 2,
    why: "Care is not transferred until a provider of equal or higher training accepts the patient and receives a report. Leaving sooner risks abandonment.",
